  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "The small medium green to light green leaves have three to five very narrow lobes separated almost entirely to the base. The lobes are elongate-lanceolate, tapering to a narrow tip. They twist sideways, curl up or down, or become slightly sickle-shaped. The margins are complex—deeply toothed to lobulate or combinations of both. The entire appearance of the foliage is disorganized but attractive. New leaves have a red overtone, which may persist around the margins. This compact dwarf is semiprostrate in habit. It eventually reaches about 3 ft. (1 m) high and wide. The name means \"one's own style or manner,\" aptly describing this cultivar's distinctive foliage."
  },
